  "title": "εἰμί, 'to be', and first sentences",
  "note": "εἰμί (I am): εἰμί, εἶ, ἐστί(ν), ἐσμέν, ἐστέ, εἰσί(ν); ἦν means 'was'. All but εἶ are enclitics: they lean on the word before and often lose their accent (Ἐγώ εἰμι). εἰμί links two nominatives, and the one with the article is the subject: θεὸς ἦν ὁ λόγος, 'the Word was God'. The verb 'is' is often left out.",
